## Project Overview
This Python program helps people manage a grocery shopping list.
For Project 2, I separated the original program into modules, added 
a class, added JSON saving and loading , and created automated tests.

## Features
- Add grocery items
- reject blank names and duplicate items regardless of capitalization.
- View numbered items and their purchased status.
- Mark items as purchased
- Reomve items
- View total, purchased, and remaining counts.
- Automatically save after changes
- Restore saved items when the program starts.
- Handle invalid input and report file errors.

## How to Run
1. Install Python 3.
2. Open the project folder in VS Code.
3. Open the terminal.
4. Run:

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Start the program:

```bash
python grocery_checklist.py
```

## Testing

Run the automated tests:

```bash
python -m pytest -q
```

All 11 tests passed

## Python Concepts Used
- Functions, arguments, and return values
- Separate modules
- Classes, objects, attributes, and methods
- File reading and writing
- JSON saving and loading
- Exception handling
- Automated testing with pytest

## File Organization

- grocery_checklist.py: Menu and user input
- shopping_list.py: Class that manages grocery items
- storage.py: Saves and loads grocery data
- test_shopping_list.py: Automated tests

## Design 

I separated the menu, list management, and storage to make the program easier to maintain and test. Inheritance was unnecessary because the program only needs one type of shopping list.

